A sweep trusts an entry's size before its CRC can vouch for it: one corrupt
byte names an entry running past the file, and the sweep reads (and
allocates) up to 4 GiB for it. Reverts the bound #36 and ed3ad5df added.
Guarded-by: "resume() does not trust an entry size that runs past the file"

